  "description": "The Welcome Garden brings a sense of nature into everyday modern living. Reflecting local ecology and geology, informal clumps of indigenous flowering plants weave between naturalistic layers of wood and rock. It reads as natural rather than designed — enhancing a distinct sense of place. Year-round flowering offers constant interest and supports pollinators such as bees, butterflies and birds, with nectar and pollen sources sustaining local ecosystems across the front and rear gardens.",
